    "lastCommit": {
      "id": "6da8836f83fcffceba9982d196e82a7aefcb472a",
      "message": "[ota-hal] OTA-1730 \u2014 the hint points somewhere you can still go\n\nAudit item 4: every \"do X to unlock Y\" has to agree with the predicate that\nactually unlocks it. One mismatch, and the module was already carrying its own\ncorrect answer.\n\n\u26a0\u26a0 `afterGuardianWall` and `afterApexWall` are the Arbiter's \"try something else\"\nlines \u2014 the ones that fire after a SECOND wall, whose entire job is to name a road\nthe player has not exhausted. Both branch on a tower and say so out loud:\n\n    \"You've heard what they bring down from the old Towers, haven't you?\"\n    \"the climbers' summits pay better still\"\n\nThey branched on `knowsATower`, which is TRUE of a tower the player has ALREADY\nTOPPED. So a player who bought one chart and crested that tower \u2014 an ordinary\nmid-game state, there are five climbs \u2014 was sent back to finished content by the\none line meant to unstick them.\n\n\u26a0\u26a0\u26a0 THE RIGHT PREDICATE WAS SIXTY LINES BELOW, AND ALREADY USED CORRECTLY. The\nvendor rumour has required `knowsAnUncrestedTower` all along. One module, two\nanswers to \"does this player have a tower to climb\", and the hints took the loose\none. TEXT WRONG / ENGINE RIGHT \u2014 so the engine's own stricter answer is now the\nonly one any hint decides on.\n\n\u26a0 `knowsATower` survives as an exported helper; a future caller may legitimately\nwant \"known at all\". What is gone is anything BRANCHING on it, which the suite\npins so the loose answer cannot creep back into a hint.\n\n\u26a0 THE OTHER HINTS I CHECKED AGREE. The main-quest ladder is generated from\n`LOST_CAPITAL_LOCATIONS` itself so it cannot drift; the descent hint names the Mud\nFlood Nexus, which is exactly what `reached_nexus` keys on (OTA-430 fixed that one\nalready); `weaponIsStale` reads the equipped weapon and the Core count it claims\nto. One dead branch noted and left alone: `phaseHint` has a `nexus` case and\nnothing anywhere assigns `phase: 'nexus'`, so that string is unreachable \u2014 no\nplayer can be misled by a line they cannot see, and deleting a phase from the\nunion is a bigger change than the finding justifies.\n\n19 gates green. Complete surface: 1208 suites, 12468 tests, 0 failures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
      "dateCreated": "2026-09-07T02:42:57Z",
